{{- /*
What the tool server says to an agent, one template per kind of answer. Go passes data and no
text. A role, a status or a delivery arrives spelled as its enum is (names.Spell), so a template
branches on the enum's own words.
*/ -}}

{{- define "oneof" -}}
Give exactly one of {{list .Fields}}{{if .Doc}} ({{.Doc}}){{end}}.
{{- end -}}

{{- define "arguments" -}}
The arguments of {{.Tool}} are wrong:
{{range .Problems}}- {{template "problem" .}}
{{end}}Fix them against the tool's input schema and call again.
{{- end -}}

{{- define "problem" -}}
{{- if eq .Kind "unknown" -}}
unknown field `{{.Field}}`: this tool takes only {{.Want}}
{{- else if eq .Kind "type" -}}
`{{.Field}}` must be {{.Want}}
{{- else if eq .Kind "enum" -}}
{{if .Got}}`{{.Field}}` is `{{.Got}}`, which is not one of: {{.Want}}{{else}}`{{.Field}}` must be one of: {{.Want}}{{end}}
{{- else if eq .Kind "required" -}}
`{{.Field}}` is required{{if .Detail}}: {{.Detail}}{{end}}
{{- else if eq .Kind "group" -}}
{{if .Field}}`{{.Field}}`: g{{else}}G{{end}}ive exactly one of {{.Want}}{{if .Doc}} ({{.Doc}}){{end}}
{{- else -}}
{{if .Field}}`{{.Field}}`: {{end}}{{.Detail}}
{{- end -}}
{{- end -}}

{{- define "wrong_role_body" -}}
You are a {{.Role}}, so your handoff goes in the `{{.Role}}` field and in no other, and you gave `{{.Given}}`: call post_handoff again with the `{{.Role}}` field.
{{- end -}}

{{- define "missing_role_body" -}}
Your handoff has no `{{.Role}}` field, which is the body for a {{.Role}}: call post_handoff again with it.
{{- end -}}

{{- define "spawn_agent" -}}
started agent {{.Agent}}. It will post a handoff when it is done; list_agents shows where it stands.
{{- end -}}

{{- define "send_message" -}}
message {{.Message}} is {{if eq .Delivery "steered"}}steered into the agent's running turn
{{- else if eq .Delivery "new_turn"}}starting the agent's next turn
{{- else if eq .Delivery "queued"}}queued until the agent's turn ends
{{- else if eq .Delivery "rejected"}}rejected
{{- else}}on its way{{end}}.
{{- end -}}

{{- define "stop_agent" -}}
agent {{.Agent}} is being stopped.
{{- end -}}

{{- define "post_handoff" -}}
handoff sent to your lead. You are done: end your turn.
{{- end -}}

{{- define "post_report" -}}
report sent to the operator.
{{- end -}}

{{- define "list_agents" -}}
{{- if not .Agents -}}
Your run has no agents.
{{- else -}}
The agents of your run:
{{range .Agents}}- {{.ID}}{{if .Self}} (you){{end}}: {{.Role}}{{if .Plan}}, plan {{.Plan}}{{end}}, {{template "status" .Status}}{{if .Parent}}, started by {{.Parent}}{{end}}
{{end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- end -}}

{{- define "status" -}}
{{- if eq . "launching" -}}starting its session
{{- else if eq . "active" -}}working on a turn
{{- else if eq . "waiting" -}}waiting for its subagents
{{- else if eq . "idle" -}}idle, between turns
{{- else if eq . "ended" -}}finished, its session closed
{{- else if eq . "failed" -}}failed
{{- else if eq . "lost" -}}lost, its session went away
{{- else -}}in an unknown state
{{- end -}}
{{- end -}}

{{- define "transport_refused" -}}
the orchestrator refused this session ({{.Message}}): stop and tell the operator; do not retry
{{- end -}}

{{- define "transport_rejected" -}}
the orchestrator rejected the request ({{.Message}}): fix the arguments and call again
{{- end -}}

{{- define "transport_unanswered" -}}
the orchestrator did not answer ({{.Message}}): call list_agents to see whether your last call took effect, then repeat it only if it did not
{{- end -}}

{{- define "no_such_tool" -}}
there is no tool `{{.Name}}`: the tools you have are {{.Tools}}
{{- end -}}

{{- define "tool_not_for_role" -}}
{{.Name}} is not available to a {{.Role}}: the tools you have are {{.Tools}}
{{- end -}}
